<%# The turn-posting form. Shown only to the current_turn_user; everyone else sees a
    "waiting" note (or a concluded note). VIEWER-SCOPED: takes an explicit `viewer:`
    local, because `current_user` is undefined in a broadcast render context and using
    it here would blank the composer on every broadcast. Local: debate, viewer (defaults
    to current_user in the request context). Wrapped in the pinned dom_id so the
    Turbo-Stream replace lands here — the debate_composer controller refocuses the field
    on both first paint and that post-turn replace.

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.5) —
    docs/design-system/components/debate/TurnComposer.prompt.md. The form surface is
    `ui/_card`, and `data:` carries `data-controller` onto the card element itself: that
    attribute is the reason `ui/_card` has a `data:` local at all (its header names this
    file), and the Stimulus controller must stay on the same element it was on. The
    field keeps its own `debate-composer-target`.

    `padded:` is NOT used — TurnComposer.jsx sets a uniform `var(--space-4)` box, so
    `class: "p-4"` is spelled instead. That is the one combination `ui/_card`'s header
    forbids mixing: `padded:` would emit `py-3`, and a same-family utility resolves by
    bundle order rather than call order, so the flag would silently beat the `p-4` this
    card wants.

    The textarea keeps `border-light-grey` and its indigo focus border — that IS the
    design system's boxed field ("The boxed variant borders light-grey and turns indigo
    on focus", TextAreaField.prompt.md) — and keeps `.debate-composer-field`, which
    carries `field-sizing: content` from the `@layer components` block in
    app/assets/tailwind/application.css. Do not inline that CSS and do not drop `rows`:
    it is the min-height fallback where `field-sizing` is unsupported.

    The waiting and concluded notes are plain 14px-muted centred sentences with no card
    behind them, exactly as TurnComposer.jsx renders its two non-form states. %>
<% viewer = local_assigns.fetch(:viewer) { current_user } %>
<div id="<%= dom_id(debate, :composer) %>" class="my-4">
  <% if debate.active? && debate.current_turn_user == viewer %>
    <%= render layout: "ui/card", locals: {class: "p-4", data: {controller: "debate-composer"}} do %>
      <%= form_with url: debate_turns_path(debate.slug), method: :post do |f| %>
        <%= f.text_area :body, rows: 3, required: true, "aria-label": "Your turn",
              data: {"debate-composer-target": "field"},
              placeholder: "Make your argument…",
              class: "debate-composer-field w-full resize-none rounded border border-light-grey p-2 text-black focus:outline-none focus:border-primary" %>
        <div class="text-right mt-2">
          <%= f.submit "Post turn", class: ds_button_classes(variant: :outline, tone: "primary", size: :md) %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  <% elsif debate.active? %>
    <p class="text-grey text-center py-3">Waiting for @<%= debate.current_turn_user&.username %>…</p>
  <% elsif debate.concluded? %>
    <p class="text-grey text-center py-3">This debate has concluded.</p>
  <% end %>
</div>
